// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Wisp 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3081993255" "Wisps are intelligent and capable leaders within the army of the Rularuu. Despite their frail appearance, they're quite tough and resilient to physical attacks, although they hate to feel the touch of another living being upon their flesh."
// DisplayNames :
"P3132871478" "Wisps"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Wisps_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3913158896" "The Wisps are always in flight, floating about from one place to another with surprising speed. When seen from a distance, they are really quite beautiful, but at close range their psychic attacks can rend even the most disciplined mind to shreds."
// DisplayNames :
"P3720916370" "Wisp Oppressor"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Wisps_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P295854679" "The most powerful Wisps have expanded the powers of their mind so greatly that they can, in small ways, affect space itself. They can seal off their enemies in small pockets of space, rendering them unable to attack or aid allies. They can also bend space around themselves, creating a powerful Dispersion Bubble that protects all those within it."
// DisplayNames :
"P479031422" "Wisp Overlord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Sentry 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1030350382" "These hideous creatures watch over the entirety of the Shadow Shard. Their giant eyeballs serve not only as a mechanism for exceptional sight, but also as their primary weapon. Regrettably, standing behind a Sentry is no safer than standing in front. Their thorn blasts can tear a hero to shreds, and they seem to be aware of everything around them."
// DisplayNames :
"P2100485936" "Watcher"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Sentry_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P625132151" "The denizens of the Shadow Shard have learned never to look a Sentry directly in the eye. By doing so, they become vulnerable to the Sentries' Paralytic Gaze, which can hold a person in place, unable to defend himself."
// DisplayNames :
"P1645815473" "Observer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Sentry_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1416299890" "The Sentries may look like mindless monsters, but their army is organized and adept. At Firebase Zulu it is theorized that the Sentries communicate through some form of telepathy, since their leaders are able to instantly summon reinforcements when things look grim."
// DisplayNames :
"P1343966772" "Overseer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Natterling 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1563403059" "Natterlings travel in large packs, hopping about the floating islands and mystic causeways of the Shadow Shard looking for intruders. They're very good scavengers, and any piece of technology or any living thing they find they'll scoop up and bring back to their masters."
// DisplayNames :
"P3718874704" "Natterling"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Natterling_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1939520857" "What are Natterlings made of? No one can truly say. Their twisted bodies seem to be composed of all manner of matter, from the flesh of Brutes to the strange jewel-like Kora fruit. In battle, the Natterlings will shoot gouts of this amalgamated material at their enemies, causing great damage and a very unpleasant smell."
// DisplayNames :
"P3670816766" "Bull Natterling"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Natterling_Lt_Merged 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1681450468" "Like all the denizens of the Shadow Shard, the Natterlings are well-adapted for survival. When threatened, two of the creatures can merge into a single, much more powerful Natterling. This poses a serious problem to heroes hoping to win a war or attrition."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Natterling_Lt_Spawner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Ruladak 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2885056123" "The leader of the Brutes is a most fearsome tyrant. Ruladak's robe is decorated with gems torn from the Brutes that have displeased him. The removal of the gem result's in the Brute's immediate death and eternal dishonor, a fact that troubles Ruladak not in the slightest."
// DisplayNames :
"P438763448" "Aspect of Rularuu"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Rularuu_Cathedral_Lanaru 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2111174074" "The demented consciousness of Lanaru the Mad is so twisted by rage that it has wrenched itself free of Rularuu. His psychic instability has manifested as a permanent storm that surrounds his castle and himself."

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

